# venueplay.com.au cache rules (Cloudflare Pages).
#
# This site had no _headers file, which is why new deploys only showed up in an
# incognito window: browsers were serving the old cached HTML. The rule below makes
# every page and app file revalidate with the server before it is used, so venues
# always get the latest version (a quick 304 when nothing changed).
#
# We use "no-cache" (revalidate), not "no-store" (never cache), on purpose: the home
# page and the musical game load /data/musical-library.json in the browser, and
# no-store would force that whole file to download again every single time.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  # Basic hardening. SAMEORIGIN rather than DENY because /tv embeds the game screens
  # in an iframe from this same site, and DENY would black out the venue TV.
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# HOW THIS FILE ACTUALLY BEHAVES, because two wrong assumptions have now been tested against
# the live site and both cost time:
#
# 1. Cloudflare Pages MERGES every rule that matches, it does not pick the most specific one.
#    Proof: /app/vp-session.js came back with "no-cache, must-revalidate" three times over, once
#    each from /*, /*.js and /app/*.js. So a later rule cannot override /*, it can only add to it.
# 2. Because of that, the /logos/* rule below DOES NOT WORK and cannot be made to work while /*
#    sets Cache-Control: per RFC 9111 a no-cache anywhere in the field forces revalidation, so
#    the logos revalidate every time despite saying immutable.
#
# That is a deliberate trade, not an oversight. Dropping Cache-Control from /* would let the logo
# rule win, but /* is the only pattern that reaches the extensionless routes Pages actually serves
# (/tv, /play, /app/billing): a /*.html rule matches none of them, and a venue TV or console stuck
# on a stale cached page is a far worse problem than a logo that revalidates. The logos are a few
# KB and return 304s. Leave it alone unless every clean URL is enumerated here first.
#
# /app/*.js is gone because /*.js already covers it; it only ever added a duplicate header.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Kept for the day /* stops setting Cache-Control. Currently merged away: see note above.
/logos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# llms.txt is a plain-language summary of this site for AI assistants. Served as
# text/plain so a crawler reads it rather than being offered a download, and
# cached briefly because it changes about as often as the homepage copy does.
/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
